x_SWI_2, y_SWI_2 = get_pin_location(symbol_ref="SW1", pin_name="2")

# Connect the two pins
connect_pins("SW1", "1", "SW1", "2")
```

Because both pins sit on the same symbol, the wire will be a short straight line, and the schematic will look clean.

**Why the rotation/mirror choices were made**

- The SW_Push symbol comes in a standard orientation with pin 1 on the right side and pin 2 on the left side.  
- Rotating it would simply swap the positions of the pins, forcing the wire to cross the symbol and clutter the drawing.  
- Mirroring it would flip the left/right assignment, again complicating the wire path.  
- Therefore rotation = 0° and mirror = None give the simplest layout.

